act our business, financial condition, and results of operations;","block":374,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001704292-26-000015","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001704292","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1704292/000170429226000015/zlab-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1a20fe635477516d7af0b9390aac630239606fa43e70f07e4aceda6712f39294.bin","sha256":"1a20fe635477516d7af0b9390aac630239606fa43e70f07e4aceda6712f39294"}},{"id":"ec8291bf74c16630890492123ece81bfe6e1c8d249500e3bcacd2bd85b07b751","quote":"•If we are unable to obtain and maintain intellectual property protection for our products and product candidates (e.g., through patent property rights), or if the scope of such intellectual property rights obtained is not sufficiently broad, third parties may compete directly against us;","context":"•We rely on third parties to conduct our pre-clinical and clinical trials. If these third parties do not successfully carry out their contractual duties or meet expected deadlines, we may not be able to obtain regulatory approval for or commercialize our products or product candidates, on the anticipated timeline or at all, and our business could be substantially harmed;","section":"•Changes in relations between the United States and China, as well as relations between China and other countries, may adversely impact our business, financial condition, and results of operations;","block":375,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001704292-26-000015","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001704292","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1704292/000170429226000015/zlab-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1a20fe635477516d7af0b9390aac630239606fa43e70f07e4aceda6712f39294.bin","sha256":"1a20fe635477516d7af0b9390aac6302